{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "a01",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 7,
      "estimated_minutes": 15,
      "reason": "The reviewer must decide whether “undefined for sales to affiliates” identifies d01’s actual-proceeds-versus-market-value dispute without stating that distinction, which the court expressly resolved. The struck-cost language also requires separating the net-versus-gross objection from the downstream-marketing question in d02."
    },
    {
      "id": "a02",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 22,
      "reason": "The assertion that the statutory trigger has “no applicable boundary in Pennsylvania” requires verification beyond the quoted clause, and “such well” requires checking against the court’s “such unit.” Even then, the reviewer must determine whether “both ... indeterminate” identifies the applicability problem in d03, the density-calculation problem in d04, or only a different size-limit objection."
    },
    {
      "id": "a03",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 7,
      "estimated_minutes": 15,
      "reason": "The work is deciding what “undefined for affiliate sales” says about the royalty base: it does not specify the actual-proceeds-versus-market-value distinction that d05 addresses and the court resolves. The reviewer must also disentangle the struck-cost objection from d06’s question about an express downstream-marketing duty."
    },
    {
      "id": "a04",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "reason": "The reviewer must verify the claimed absence of an applicable Pennsylvania boundary and determine how that assertion supports the description’s conclusion. “The density duty [is] indeterminate” leaves unclear whether the complaint concerns which units are covered under d07, how wells are counted under d08, or uncertainty derived solely from the asserted size-limit problem."
    },
    {
      "id": "a05",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 7,
      "estimated_minutes": 15,
      "reason": "The reviewer must interpret the general affiliate-sale objection against d09’s specific distinction between actual receipts and market value, rather than treating the shared phrase “price paid to Lessee” as sufficient by itself. The net-versus-gross assertion adds a separate comparison with d10’s use of the deleted cost language to interpret “marketed.”"
    },
    {
      "id": "a06",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "reason": "Checking the Pennsylvania-law assertion requires more than reading the clause, while the concluding statement does not explain why the density duty is indeterminate. The reviewer must then test that general complaint against both d11’s coverage question and d12’s complete-acreage-group question before assessing the no-match call."
    },
    {
      "id": "a07",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 7,
      "estimated_minutes": 15,
      "reason": "The difficult step is determining whether “undefined for affiliate sales” names d13’s royalty-base dispute despite omitting the actual-proceeds-versus-market-value alternatives that the court distinguished. The reviewer must separately assess what the struck-cost discussion contributes, given d14’s different focus on an express marketing obligation."
    },
    {
      "id": "a08",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "reason": "The description combines a Pennsylvania-law claim needing verification with a general assertion that the density duty is indeterminate. After checking that claim, the reviewer still must decide whether the description reaches d15’s all-units-versus-larger-units problem or instead complains about the size exception or density calculation."
    },
    {
      "id": "a09",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 7,
      "estimated_minutes": 15,
      "reason": "The reviewer must decide how much substantive meaning to give “undefined for affiliate sales,” which names the relevant phrase but not d17’s distinction between actual proceeds and market value. The deleted-cost assertion must also be separated from d18’s downstream-marketing issue rather than allowing the two royalty objections to blur together."
    },
    {
      "id": "a10",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "reason": "The reviewer must check the assertion about Pennsylvania’s lack of an applicable boundary and trace its connection to the alleged indeterminacy of the density duty. The description never specifies whether that indeterminacy concerns d19’s coverage of smaller units, d20’s acreage-group calculation, or only the asserted uncertainty in permissible unit size."
    }
  ]
}
